						"description": "**Purpose:**\nThis request updates the details of an existing category in the system. It is typically used by administrators or authorized users to modify category information such as the name and description.\n\n**Endpoint:**\n```\nPUT {{baseUrl}}/api/categories/:categoryId\n```\n- `{{baseUrl}}` is a variable representing the base URL of the API server.\n- `:categoryId` should be replaced with the unique identifier of the category you wish to update (e.g., `1`).\n\n**Request Body:**\nThe request body must be in JSON format and include the following fields:\n- `categoryName` (string): The new or updated name of the category. Example: `\"Electronics & Gadgets\"`\n- `catDescription` (string): A description of the category. Example: `\"All electronic devices and accessories\"`\n\n**Example Request Body:**\n```\n{\n  \"categoryName\": \"Electronics & Gadgets\",\n  \"catDescription\": \"All electronic devices and accessories\"\n}\n```\n\n**Notes:**\n- Ensure that the category ID in the URL corresponds to an existing category.\n- Both fields in the request body are required.\n- The request may require authentication or specific permissions depending on your API's security settings.\n- A successful update typically returns a 200 OK status with the updated category details."
